{
  "id": "leetcode-366",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "approved",
  "title": "Find Leaves of Binary Tree",
  "summary": "Starting with the root of a binary tree, gather all leaf nodes.",
  "statement": "Starting with the root of a binary tree, gather all leaf nodes. Remove these leaf nodes. Continue this process until the tree is completely empty.",
  "constraints": [
    "The tree has 1 to 100 nodes; -100 <= each node value <= 100.",
    "Return one list of values per simultaneous leaf-removal round, earliest round first. Values within a round may be in any order, but repeated values from different nodes must be preserved.",
    "You need not physically modify the tree; report the rounds as if all current leaves were removed together."
  ],
  "topics": [
    "trees",
    "recursion",
    "depth-first-search",
    "dynamic-programming"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [],
  "signature": {
    "name": "leaf_removal_rounds",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "root",
        "annotation": "TreeNode | None",
        "adapter": "treenode",
        "source_parameter": null
      }
    ],
    "returns": "list[list[int]]",
    "return_adapter": "raw",
    "node_policy": "values",
    "result_mode": "return",
    "mutated_parameter": null,
    "immutable_parameters": []
  },
  "starter_code": "# Data structure supplied to this problem.\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        val: int = 0,\n        left: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n        right: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n    ):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n\ndef leaf_removal_rounds(root: TreeNode | None) -> list[list[int]]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n",
  "reference_solution": "def leaf_removal_rounds(root):\n    rounds = []\n    def height(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return -1\n        level = 1+max(height(node.left),height(node.right))\n        if level == len(rounds):\n            rounds.append([])\n        rounds[level].append(node.val)\n        return level\n    height(root)\n    return rounds\n",
  "brute_force_solution": null,
  "known_wrong_solutions": [
    "def leaf_removal_rounds(root):\n    rounds = []\n    def height(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return -1\n        level = 1+min(height(node.left),height(node.right))\n        if level == len(rounds):\n            rounds.append([])\n        rounds[level].append(node.val)\n        return level\n    height(root)\n    return rounds\n",
    "def leaf_removal_rounds(root):\n    rounds = []\n    def height(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return -1\n        level = 1+max(height(node.left),height(node.right))\n        if level == len(rounds):\n            rounds.append([])\n        rounds[level].append(node.val)\n        return level\n    height(root)\n    return rounds[::-1]\n"
  ],
  "target_time_complexity": "O(n)",
  "target_space_complexity": "O(n) output and O(height) recursion",
  "estimated_minutes": 35,
  "rubric": {
    "algorithmic_insight": 2,
    "prerequisites": 1,
    "implementation": 1,
    "performance_pressure": 1,
    "edge_cases": 0
  },
  "hints": [
    "A node becomes a leaf only after both of its child subtrees have disappeared.",
    "Its removal round is one plus the maximum child removal round; missing children have round -1.",
    "Recursively compute child heights, append node.val to rounds[1+max(left,right)], and return that height.",
    "Postorder groups each node by its height above the deepest descendant leaf. Equal values remain separate occurrences."
  ],
  "editorial": "The first round contains leaves, whose height is zero. An internal node disappears one round after its last child, giving 1+max(child heights). One postorder traversal assigns each node to exactly one chronological group. The comparator ignores order only inside each group, never across rounds, and preserves duplicate counts. The independent oracle repeatedly removes actual leaf paths from a JSON-level tree map.",
